  "facts": [
    "The Eurasia Tunnel, opened on 20 December 2016, stretches 5.4 km beneath the Bosphorus, reaching a maximum depth of 106 m and cutting through 3.4 km of seabed in just 479 calendar days.",
    "Designed by Parsons Brinckerhoff with seismic joints limiting displacement to ±50 mm, the tunnel’s 13.7 m diameter TBM set a world record for cutterhead power at 33 kW/m² during excavation.",
    "Tolling began on 22 December 2016, charging ₺156 for cars during daytime and offering a 50 % discount after sunset, making it Istanbul’s fastest 5‑minute cross‑continental link."
  ],
